WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.799 --> 00:00:20.223
climbed onto the team bus on Friday to go to the game at West Middle School, home of

2
00:00:20.243 --> 00:00:20.763
the Bandits.

3
00:00:24.746 --> 00:00:27.028
He took a seat in the front and opened his math book.

4
00:00:28.649 --> 00:00:31.392
Dell slid in beside him and laughed when he saw the book.

5
00:00:33.089 --> 00:00:35.250
"You're doing math homework before the game?"

6
00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:39.173
"My last quiz pulled my grade down," mumbled Patrick.

7
00:00:39.973 --> 00:00:42.655
He was embarrassed to admit how poorly he was doing in math.

8
00:00:43.496 --> 00:00:44.617
He quickly closed the book.

9
00:00:45.997 --> 00:00:47.098
"But it's not a big deal.

10
00:00:47.478 --> 00:00:48.479
Let's talk baseball."

11
00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.842
At the ballpark Patrick carried his equipment bag to the dugout.

12
00:00:56.204 --> 00:00:59.647
He probably wouldn't need his catcher's equipment—unless Mickey got hurt.

13
00:01:00.447 --> 00:01:01.448
Patrick shook his head.

14
00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:03.762
He wanted the starting catcher spot.

15
00:01:04.642 --> 00:01:07.725
But he wanted to win it fairly, not because someone else was injured.

16
00:01:08.366 --> 00:01:10.087
He ran out to left field to warm up.

17
00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:17.294
Before the fifth inning, Patrick caught three flies and fielded some easy grounders.

18
00:01:18.855 --> 00:01:24.240
His playing was nothing spectacular, but it was nice to hear his father cheering, even from a distance.

19
00:01:25.341 --> 00:01:28.664
Now it was the top of the sixth inning, and Patrick was up to bat.

20
00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:33.363
He flexed his fingers inside his batting gloves, trying to loosen up.

21
00:01:35.184 --> 00:01:38.928
He had popped out his first time at bat, and he got tagged out at first base on

22
00:01:38.948 --> 00:01:39.908
his second time at bat.

23
00:01:40.749 --> 00:01:44.792
He faced the pitcher again, every fiber in his body wanting a hit.

24
00:01:45.693 --> 00:01:47.074
His hands tightened on the bat.

25
00:01:47.775 --> 00:01:48.756
His muscles tensed.

26
00:01:49.556 --> 00:01:52.839
Crack! The ball popped over the right field stands.

27
00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:59.475
Foul. Patrick stepped out from the batter's box and imagined that he was the opposing catcher crouched behind

28
00:01:59.515 --> 00:02:00.016
home plate.

29
00:02:01.016 --> 00:02:05.059
As a catcher, Patrick would think, "This batter is trying too hard.

30
00:02:05.839 --> 00:02:06.440
He's tense.

31
00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:08.201
He'll swing at the next one."

32
00:02:11.203 --> 00:02:15.686
Patrick stepped back into the box, carefully positioned his feet, and raised the bat.

33
00:02:18.288 --> 00:02:21.910
The pitch was outside the plate, and he let it go, without swinging.

34
00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:24.392
"Ball!" said the umpire.

35
00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:26.801
"Nice job," he told himself.

36
00:02:27.602 --> 00:02:28.903
The next pitch was high.

37
00:02:30.204 --> 00:02:32.486
Patrick didn't swing again—another ball.

38
00:02:33.446 --> 00:02:34.587
Patrick hid his grin.

39
00:02:34.607 --> 00:02:38.610
"Now the pitcher will try to whiz the ball past me," he thought.

40
00:02:39.351 --> 00:02:42.113
Fastball. Crack!

41
00:02:43.114 --> 00:02:44.855
The bat connected and Patrick ran.

42
00:02:47.677 --> 00:02:51.440
He rounded first base, glancing at Coach, who gave him the signal to go.

43
00:02:52.824 --> 00:02:55.945
Patrick's legs churned and then he slid into second base.

44
00:02:55.965 --> 00:03:00.667
"Safe!" called the umpire.

45
00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:04.549
Patrick brushed off his pants as the crowd cheered.

46
00:03:04.569 --> 00:03:07.750
"A double," he thought.

47
00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:10.691
"Yes!" Mickey was up next.

48
00:03:12.172 --> 00:03:16.474
Patrick inched toward third base, his eyes on Daniel, the third-base coach.

49
00:03:17.154 --> 00:03:18.215
His adrenaline pumped.

50
00:03:19.375 --> 00:03:21.436
He might get to home, if he was fast enough.

51
00:03:22.432 --> 00:03:23.673
He didn't have to worry about it.

52
00:03:24.113 --> 00:03:26.115
Mickey slammed the ball over the fence.

53
00:03:27.676 --> 00:03:30.217
Homerun! The score was 4-4.

54
00:03:31.238 --> 00:03:34.460
The next Dragon hitter struck out, giving the team three outs.

55
00:03:35.121 --> 00:03:36.702
Patrick ran back to left field.

56
00:03:36.722 --> 00:03:39.804
"Batter up!"

57
00:03:40.224 --> 00:03:41.065
called the umpire.

58
00:03:42.085 --> 00:03:47.549
From his spot in left field, Patrick couldn't see the other fielders, and Dell looked like a flagpole

59
00:03:47.589 --> 00:03:48.109
on the mound.

60
00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:51.592
He couldn't read the signal Mickey put down for the pitch.

61
00:03:53.172 --> 00:03:57.115
Crack! A hard grounder zinged past Gene on third base.

62
00:03:58.216 --> 00:03:59.877
Patrick ran forward and scooped it up.

63
00:04:01.898 --> 00:04:03.119
He shot the ball to first.

64
00:04:05.421 --> 00:04:08.162
As soon as it left his hand, he knew it was high.

65
00:04:08.943 --> 00:04:13.046
If the ball went over Buck's head, the Bandits runner might even get a double.

66
00:04:13.946 --> 00:04:15.868
Buck leaped up and brought down the ball.

67
00:04:17.209 --> 00:04:18.630
The runner was safe on first.

68
00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:20.311
"Nice catch, Buck!"

69
00:04:20.771 --> 00:04:21.151
yelled Mr.

70
00:04:22.468 --> 00:04:24.369
Deboe. Patrick scuffed the grass with his toe.

71
00:04:26.831 --> 00:04:28.172
Buck had saved him on that one.

72
00:04:28.913 --> 00:04:32.435
Patrick wished he was playing where he belonged, behind home plate.

73
00:04:33.316 --> 00:04:35.797
When he was catching, he didn't— Crack!

74
00:04:37.339 --> 00:04:40.421
Too late Patrick realized the next batter had gotten a hit.

75
00:04:41.081 --> 00:04:43.723
Patrick spotted the fly ball coming toward him and ran.

76
00:04:43.743 --> 00:04:47.986
"Faster!" he told himself.

77
00:04:48.707 --> 00:04:50.408
He dove as the ball came down.

78
00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:55.001
It nicked the tip of his glove and bounced off.

79
00:04:57.241 --> 00:05:01.483
Patrick scrambled to his feet, picked up the ball, and rocketed it to second.

80
00:05:03.143 --> 00:05:04.543
The umpire spread his arms.

81
00:05:04.563 --> 00:05:07.624
"Safe!" "Good try!"

82
00:05:07.944 --> 00:05:08.645
somebody yelled.

83
00:05:08.665 --> 00:05:13.426
"Not good enough," Patrick thought as he jogged back to position.

84
00:05:14.466 --> 00:05:17.147
The next batter hit a double and brought one runner in.

85
00:05:19.147 --> 00:05:20.948
The Bandits fans went wild.

86
00:05:24.284 --> 00:05:27.347
After seven innings the Dragons lost, 5-4.

87
00:05:28.047 --> 00:05:29.068
Coach gathered the team.

88
00:05:29.088 --> 00:05:30.870
"You fought hard.

89
00:05:31.450 --> 00:05:35.634
We won't win every game, but teamwork will carry us to the championship.

90
00:05:36.394 --> 00:05:38.276
Everybody has to give all they've got."

91
00:05:38.296 --> 00:05:41.999
"This loss is my fault," thought Patrick.

92
00:05:42.679 --> 00:05:45.902
He'd been moping about playing left field instead of watching the batter.

93
00:05:46.883 --> 00:05:49.685
His head wasn't in the game, and it had cost the team.

94
00:05:50.886 --> 00:05:52.768
The players started heading for the parking lot.

95
00:05:55.552 --> 00:05:56.893
"Look!" said Dell.

96
00:05:56.913 --> 00:05:58.815
"It's got a tail now!"

97
00:05:59.936 --> 00:06:01.317
Patrick glanced at the van.

98
00:06:01.917 --> 00:06:02.618
Dell was right.

99
00:06:03.098 --> 00:06:06.161
The van now had a tail—and it was wagging!

100
00:06:07.202 --> 00:06:08.182
Patrick groaned.

101
00:06:08.943 --> 00:06:12.606
This had to be what Dad and Daniel were working on in the garage last weekend.

102
00:06:12.626 --> 00:06:15.268
"Hey, Patrick," said Buck.

103
00:06:15.288 --> 00:06:16.970
"Can I look inside the van?

104
00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:18.791
Sheila said it's really cool."

105
00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:21.173
"Me too," said Gene.

106
00:06:21.774 --> 00:06:22.534
Patrick shrugged.

107
00:06:22.554 --> 00:06:24.456
"Sure. It's just a van."

108
00:06:25.716 --> 00:06:27.497
"Our dog, Bitsy, loved it!"

109
00:06:27.877 --> 00:06:28.498
said Sheila.

110
00:06:29.038 --> 00:06:30.359
"It's like a doggie spa."

111
00:06:31.219 --> 00:06:35.782
Everyone wanted to see it, so Patrick led both baseball teams to the Doggie Express van.

112
00:06:37.683 --> 00:06:40.605
Kids gathered around as his mother swung open the back doors.

113
00:06:41.285 --> 00:06:42.406
Patrick shook his head.

114
00:06:43.386 --> 00:06:44.747
Why was everyone so excited?

115
00:06:45.227 --> 00:06:47.349
It wasn't like his mom drove an ice cream truck.

116
00:06:48.169 --> 00:06:52.972
Mrs. Deboe showed off the folding tables, self-heating tub, and little doggie mirrors.

117
00:06:53.908 --> 00:06:55.549
"My beagle would love this!"

118
00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:57.130
said the Bandits pitcher.

119
00:06:58.391 --> 00:06:59.392
Somebody else laughed.

120
00:06:59.412 --> 00:07:01.274
"My boxer wouldn't like it.

121
00:07:01.614 --> 00:07:03.755
He hates water more than trips to the vet."

122
00:07:04.836 --> 00:07:08.919
The kids laughed and talked about their dogs as they walked off to find their rides or get

123
00:07:08.979 --> 00:07:09.740
back on a bus.

124
00:07:11.721 --> 00:07:12.442
Daniel and Mr.

125
00:07:12.482 --> 00:07:16.885
Deboe huddled to talk about the game while Patrick's mom put away stuff in the van.

126
00:07:19.247 --> 00:07:20.868
A few kids stood near Patrick.

127
00:07:21.856 --> 00:07:23.557
"What kind of dog do you have, Mickey?"

128
00:07:23.857 --> 00:07:24.517
asked Sheila.

129
00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:28.139
"You've probably never seen one," said Mickey.

130
00:07:28.919 --> 00:07:30.399
"Ratty's an Irish wolfhound."

131
00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:33.241
"Hey! Our dog, Bitsy, is a wolfhound!"

132
00:07:33.581 --> 00:07:34.101
said Buck.

133
00:07:35.081 --> 00:07:35.802
Mickey grinned.

134
00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:38.163
"We should get them together at the dog park."

135
00:07:38.983 --> 00:07:40.363
"A playdate for dogs!"

136
00:07:40.664 --> 00:07:41.264
Buck laughed.

137
00:07:41.724 --> 00:07:42.444
"Let's do it!"

138
00:07:43.365 --> 00:07:45.105
"What kind of dog do you have, Patrick?"

139
00:07:45.405 --> 00:07:45.966
asked Mickey.

140
00:07:46.506 --> 00:07:47.426
"Daniel has a mutt.

141
00:07:47.666 --> 00:07:49.527
I have a cat," muttered Patrick.

142
00:07:49.547 --> 00:07:52.312
"Oh, cats are cool," said Mickey.

143
00:07:52.332 --> 00:07:55.233
"Yep." Patrick stared down at the ground.

144
00:07:55.914 --> 00:08:00.716
For once he couldn't wait for his mother to start up that dumb doggy van—and take him home.
